[111.399,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what will be deleted from your AWS account:\r\n\r\n  # The master, its Elastic IP, the media nodes' auto scaling group, the security\r\n  # groups and the secrets.\r\n  # First let the media nodes go without draining their sessions.\r\n  aws autoscaling delete-lifecycle-hook --auto-scaling-group-name '$(aws cloudformation describe-stack-resource --stack-name openvidu-e2e-aws-el-a102129 --logical-resource-id MediaNodeAutoScalingGroup --query StackResourceDetail.PhysicalResourceId --output text --region eu-south-2)' --lifecycle-hook-name openvidu-media-drain --region eu-south-2\r\n  aws cloudformation delete-stack --stack-name openvidu-e2e-aws-el-a102129 --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\n  # The key pair this stack's deploy imported.\r\n  aws ec2 delete-key-pair --key-name openvidu-e2e-aws-el-a102129-key --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\n  # The template this stack's deploy staged (the bucket stays: every stack in the\r\n  # region shares it).\r\n  aws s3 rm s3://openvidu-cfn-templates-***-eu-south-2/openvidu-e2e-aws-el-a102129/ --recursive --only-show-errors --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\nWith --delete-data the S3 data bucket goes too, with your recordings and Meet data, after the stack (the template marks it Retain,\r\nso the stack alone would leave it):\r\n  aws s3 rb s3://<each data bucket of the stack> --force --region eu-south-2\r\nThe destroy leaves the per-account bucket the deploy stages its template in\r\n(openvidu-cfn-templates-<account>-<region>): every stack in the region shares it.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
